---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { CatalogueList } from "../components/react/CatalogueList.tsx";
import { loadCatalogueData } from "../lib/load-catalogue.ts";

const data = await loadCatalogueData();
const title = "Algorithm Catalogue";

export const prerender = true;
---

<Layout title={`APEx ${title}`}>
  <div class="my-14">
    <main
      class="w-full block min-h-screen sm:max-w-screen-sm md:max-w-screen-md lg:max-w-screen-lg xl:max-w-screen-xl mx-auto px-4"
    >
      <div class="max-w-screen-xl text-center mx-auto mb-10">
        <h1
          class="text-3xl md:text-5xl mb-8 pb-10 text-white after:content-[''] relative after:absolute after:w-16 after:h-[2px] after:bottom-0 after:left-1/2 after:transform after:-translate-x-1/2 after:bg-brand-teal-50"
        >
          {title}
        </h1>
        <p class="text-balance text-brand-gray-50">
          The APEx Algorithm Catalogue is a valuable and innovative resource
          that provides access to a wide range of high-quality EO services. For
          users, it offers a central place to discover EO services that meet
          their specific needs. For EO projects, it serves as an easy and
          reliable platform to showcase and offer their services to a broader
          community, fostering collaboration and wider usage of their results.
        </p>
        <details
          class="mt-6 rounded-lg border border-brand-teal-50 bg-brand-teal-80 p-5 text-left text-sm leading-6 text-white shadow-lg"
        >
          <summary
            class="cursor-pointer text-base font-semibold text-white marker:text-brand-teal-50 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-brand-teal-50"
          >
            Quality, validation, and benchmarks
          </summary>
          <div class="mt-4 border-t border-brand-teal-50/40 pt-4 text-brand-gray-50">
            <p>
              The catalogue includes EO value-adding algorithms from different
              providers (Algorithm PIs), running on different EO platforms
              (Hosting Environments), and following one of two interoperability
              best practices: openEO or EO Application Packages.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3">
              Algorithms have undergone different levels of quality assurance
              and validation. Those originating from ESA R&amp;D projects
              usually involve quality assurance and some stages of validation;
              these are marked as “validated” in the catalogue. Nevertheless,
              this does not mean an algorithm will always return a validated
              result. Applying these algorithms requires an understanding of
              their context and limitations. Algorithms labeled “community”
              were contributed by the wider EO community outside an ESA R&amp;D
              project context. They have typically undergone less quality
              assurance and validation and should be used accordingly.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3">
              In addition, APEx runs technical benchmarks on some algorithms.
              These benchmarks check that an algorithm responds, functions, and
              returns results according to a predefined application scenario.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
      <CatalogueList catalogues={data} client:only="react" />
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>
